1
00:00:00,599 --> 00:00:03,469
(applause, cheering
and whooping)

2
00:00:03,469 --> 00:00:04,769
(Howard:)Thank you.

3
00:00:04,770 --> 00:00:06,670
(Howard:)Thank you.

4
00:00:06,672 --> 00:00:08,542
(Penny:)Can he really
throw a ball?

5
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:12,610
(Leonard:)On our Quidditch
team, he...
Yeah, that's a "no."

6
00:00:12,611 --> 00:00:17,481
(Howard:)I have a message
for the young people here today.

7
00:00:17,483 --> 00:00:20,283
(Howard:)When I was asked
to throw the first pitch,

8
00:00:20,285 --> 00:00:25,385
(Howard:)a little voice in my head said
I couldn't do it.

9
00:00:25,391 --> 00:00:28,491
(Howard:)So, I practiced and practiced,

10
00:00:28,494 --> 00:00:30,564
(Howard:)and you know what?

11
00:00:30,562 --> 00:00:33,132
That little voice... (laughs)

12
00:00:33,132 --> 00:00:35,602
(Howard:)...was right, but...

13
00:00:37,202 --> 00:00:40,842
(Howard:)...then I remembered
that I'm not an athlete.

14
00:00:40,839 --> 00:00:43,209
(Howard:)I'm a scientist.

15
00:00:43,208 --> 00:00:44,508
(Howard:)So, today's

16
00:00:44,510 --> 00:00:46,910
(Howard:)first pitch will be delivered

17
00:00:46,912 --> 00:00:49,812
(Howard:)to home plate by science.

18
00:00:49,815 --> 00:00:51,385
(Stadium Announcer:)Ladies and gentlemen,

19
00:00:51,383 --> 00:00:53,753
(Howard:)boys and girls, I present to you

20
00:00:53,752 --> 00:00:59,592
(Howard:)a working prototype
of the Mars Rover!

